Theorem RL-25: logical event-pair eliminability

  Preconditions:
    - RL-24 identifies a logical owner-credit/release pair.
    - KnownSafe or both-path safety evidence is available.

  Soundness property:
    A matched pair is eliminable iff KnownSafe holds OR both directions are
    safe with no CFG multiplicity hazard. Elimination preserves exact logical
    balance and evaluator behavior.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate KnownSafe, both-safe/no-hazard, CFG-hazard, and one-path-unsafe.
    Coverage gate: 4 cases. A CFG hazard blocks elimination.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl25_pair_eliminable_conditions)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-25 eliminates only logically matched owner-credit/release pairs with KnownSafe or hazard-free bidirectional evidence
